From b37701631d9dce09a494fdccb962e47a3cb01c09 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:17:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] origin-work snapshot: a save refused for a moved
 kanban home no longer fails the remote-links read

Follow-up to the review nit on #3041 (review 5906022807, card t_01a1db0bed4a833a).

#3041 makes `remote_snapshot(cards)` refuse a save when `kanban_home()` moves while the
scope is resolved, and refuse a test process writing the live root. Both raised a bare
RuntimeError. `_legacy_remote_links()` caught only `sqlite3.Error` around the save, so a
refused save failed the whole read, against its own "must not fail this read" contract:
cold and strict reads propagated it and the sidebar would mark every row kanban_unknown.

Fix: the race now raises `SnapshotRootMoved(RuntimeError)`, and `_legacy_remote_links`
catches it alongside `sqlite3.Error`, logs "origin-work snapshot not saved; retrying on
the next change" and returns its cards. `_snapshot_saved` stays unset, so the next read
retries the save. The test-isolation tripwire (`ensure_origin_work_test_isolation`) still
raises a plain RuntimeError through the read: it exists to fail a leaking test loudly.

Proof:
- RED (on #3041's head 05c3dcede5, new test only):
  test_a_save_refused_for_a_moved_home_does_not_fail_the_remote_links_read fails with
  "RuntimeError: kanban home moved while resolving the origin-work scope".
- GREEN: test_kanban_origin_snapshot_isolation.py 6/6, including the new
  test_the_test_isolation_tripwire_still_fails_the_remote_links_read; 291 tests across
  the 17 test files referencing the snapshot or _legacy_remote_links pass;
  scripts/check --base origin/main ok.
